-- title:
--   Vanishing of Tor₁(R/(x₁,…,xₙ),M) for weakly regular sequences
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $M$ an $R$-module (both in the same universe $u$), and let $rs = [x_1,\dots,x_n]$ be a finite list of elements of $R$ which is weakly regular on $M$, i.e. for each index $i$ the element $x_i$ acts as a non-zero-divisor on the quotient $M/(x_1,\dots,x_{i-1})M$ by the submodule generated by the action of the preceding entries. Write $\mathrm{Ideal.ofList}\ rs$ for the ideal of $R$ generated by the entries of the list. The assertion is that the object obtained by applying the degree-$1$ Tor bifunctor on $\mathrm{ModuleCat}\ R$, first to the $R$-module $R/(x_1,\dots,x_n)$ and then to $M$, is a zero object of $\mathrm{ModuleCat}\ R$; that is, $\operatorname{Tor}_1^R\bigl(R/(x_1,\dots,x_n),M\bigr)=0$. Only the first Tor group is claimed to vanish: nothing is asserted about $\operatorname{Tor}_i$ for $i\ge 2$, and the list is not assumed to be regular in the strong sense (no condition that the quotients be nonzero).
--
--   This is the standard vanishing statement for the first Tor group against the quotient by a weakly regular sequence, one half of the characterisation of regular sequences by Koszul homology. It is used in the commutative-algebra layer supporting the project, notably in the flatness and freeness criteria over regular local rings ([`Module.Flat.of_isLocalHom_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_zero`](thm.html#Module.Flat.of_isLocalHom_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_zero) and [`Module.free_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_finite_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_ringKrullDim_le_two`](thm.html#Module.free_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_finite_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_ringKrullDim_le_two)) and in a smoothness argument for the Igusa scheme.
